@startuml 13_auth_rbac_sequence
!theme plain
autonumber

title TeleMed AI Platform — JWT Authentication & Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

actor User
participant "React Frontend\n(LoginPage.jsx)" as FE
participant "Auth Router\n(auth_routes.py)" as AuthRouter
participant "Security Engine\n(security.py)" as Security
participant "PostgreSQL Database\n(users / auth_sessions)" as DB
participant "Protected Route Handler\n(api/admin_routes.py)" as ProtectedRoute

User -> FE : Enter Email & Password
FE -> AuthRouter : POST /api/auth/login (json={email, password})

AuthRouter -> DB : query_user_by_email(email)
DB --> AuthRouter : User Entity (user_id, password_hash, salt, role)

AuthRouter -> Security : verify_password(plain_password, password_hash, salt)
Security --> AuthRouter : Password Verified (True)

AuthRouter -> Security : create_jwt_access_token(user_id, email, role, expires_delta)
Security --> AuthRouter : Signed JWT Bearer Token string

AuthRouter -> DB : INSERT INTO auth_sessions (token, user_id, expires_at)
DB --> AuthRouter : Session Persisted

AuthRouter --> FE : HTTP 200 OK (access_token, user_id, role, full_name)
FE -> FE : Store Token in LocalStorage & Update AuthContext State

== Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) Verification ==

User -> FE : Navigate to Protected Admin Dashboard (/admin)
FE -> ProtectedRoute : GET /api/admin/system-health (Header: Authorization: Bearer JWT)

ProtectedRoute -> Security : verify_jwt_token(token)
Security -> Security : Decode JWT & Verify Signature / Expiration
Security --> ProtectedRoute : Token Payload (user_id, role="ADMIN")

alt Role matches required endpoint permission (e.g. role == "ADMIN")
  ProtectedRoute -> DB : Fetch System Health / Observability Data
  DB --> ProtectedRoute : Metrics & Audit Summary
  ProtectedRoute --> FE : HTTP 200 OK (System Data)
  FE --> User : Render Admin Dashboard
else Role unauthorized (e.g. role == "PATIENT" trying to access Admin Route)
  Security --> ProtectedRoute : Permission Denied
  ProtectedRoute --> FE : HTTP 403 Forbidden ("Insufficient Role Privileges")
  FE --> User : Display "Access Denied" Notification
end

@enduml
